
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E : Points
BC = BA [00]
BC = BD [01]
AC = AD [02]
CE ⟂ BC [03]
AE = AC [04]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. BC = BA [00] & BC = BD [01] ⇒  B is the circumcenter of \Delta CAD [05]
002. B is the circumcenter of \Delta CAD [05] & CE ⟂ BC [03] ⇒  ∠ECA = ∠CDA [06]
003. AC = AD [02] ⇒  ∠ADC = ∠DCA [07]
004. AE = AC [04] ⇒  ∠ACE = ∠CEA [08]
005. ∠ADC = ∠DCA [07] & ∠ACE = ∠ADC [06] & ∠ACE = ∠CEA [08] ⇒  ∠CEA = ∠DCA [09]
006. ∠ECA = ∠CDA [06] & ∠CEA = ∠DCA [09] (Similar Triangles)⇒  DA:CA = DC:CE [10]
007. DA:CA = DC:CE [10] & AC = AD [02] ⇒  DC = CE
